### Core Definitions: Overloading vs Overriding

* **Method Overloading**: Defining multiple methods within the **same class** having the **same name but different parameter lists** (different count, types, or order). Overloading is resolved at **compile time** (static binding).
* **Method Overriding**: Redefining a method in a **subclass** that already exists in its **superclass** with the **exact same name and identical parameter list**. Overriding is resolved at **runtime** (dynamic binding).

---

### The Definitive Comparison Matrix

| Feature | Method Overloading | Method Overriding |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Resolution Time** | Compile-Time (Static Binding) | Runtime (Dynamic Binding) |
| **Class Scope** | Occurs within the same class | Requires inheritance across two classes |
| **Method Name** | Must be identical | Must be identical |
| **Parameters** | Must be different (count/type/order) | Must be exactly identical |
| **Return Type** | Can be different | Must be identical or covariant |
| **Access Modifiers** | Can be changed freely | Cannot be more restrictive than parent |
| **private / static** | Can overload `private` and `static` methods | Cannot override `private` or `static` methods |

---

### Side-by-Side Code Demonstration

```java
class StringFormatter {
    // 1. Method Overloading: Same name, different parameter lists
    String format(int number) {
        return "Number: " + number;
    }

    String format(String text, boolean uppercase) {
        return uppercase ? text.toUpperCase() : text.toLowerCase();
    }
}

class BaseLogger {
    // Superclass method for overriding
    void log(String message) {
        System.out.println("[INFO] " + message);
    }
}

class TimestampedLogger extends BaseLogger {
    // 2. Method Overriding: Same name, exact same parameters
    @Override
    void log(String message) {
        System.out.println("[2026-10-03 10:00:00] [INFO] " + message);
    }
}

public class ComparisonDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Overloading in action
        StringFormatter formatter = new StringFormatter();
        System.out.println(formatter.format(42));
        System.out.println(formatter.format("hello world", true));

        // Overriding in action
        BaseLogger logger = new TimestampedLogger();
        logger.log("Application started successfully");
    }
}
```

**Console Output:**
```text
Number: 42
HELLO WORLD
[2026-10-03 10:00:00] [INFO] Application started successfully
```

