practiceProblems.problemStatement:
Calculate loan interest combining overload and override from scratch:

1. Class Loan:
   - Method 1: public double calculateInterest(double principal) returning principal * 0.08 (standard 8% for 1 year)
   - Method 2 (Overload): public double calculateInterest(double principal, int months) returning principal * 0.08 * (months / 12.0)

2. Class CommercialLoan (extends Loan):
   - Method (Override): @Override public double calculateInterest(double principal) returning principal * 0.12 (12% commercial rate)

Test in Main:
Loan base = new Loan();
print 'Base Loan (1 Year): $' + base.calculateInterest(10000.0);
print 'Base Loan (6 Months): $' + base.calculateInterest(10000.0, 6);
Loan comm = new CommercialLoan();
print 'Commercial Loan: $' + comm.calculateInterest(10000.0);

practiceProblems.solutionCode:
class Loan {
    public double calculateInterest(double principal) {
        return principal * 0.08;
    }
    public double calculateInterest(double principal, int months) {
        return principal * 0.08 * (months / 12.0);
    }
}

class CommercialLoan extends Loan {
    @Override
    public double calculateInterest(double principal) {
        return principal * 0.12;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Loan loan = new Loan();
        Loan comm = new CommercialLoan();
        System.out.println("Base Loan (1 Year): $" + loan.calculateInterest(10000.0));
        System.out.println("Base Loan (6 Months): $" + loan.calculateInterest(10000.0, 6));
        System.out.println("Commercial Loan: $" + comm.calculateInterest(10000.0));
    }
}

practiceProblems.problemStatement:
Fix compiler error: 'method parseData(String) is already defined':

Bug: `int parseData(String raw)` and `double parseData(String raw)` have the same name and parameters! Java does NOT allow overloading by return type alone.

Your Task:
1. Keep `public int parseData(String raw)` returning `Integer.parseInt(raw)`.
2. Overload the second method by adding a boolean parameter: `public double parseData(String raw, boolean isDecimal)` returning `Double.parseDouble(raw)`.

Test in Main:
DataParser parser = new DataParser();
print 'Parsed Integer: ' + parser.parseData("42");
print 'Parsed Double: ' + parser.parseData("88.5", true);

practiceProblems.initialCode:
class DataParser {
    public int parseData(String raw) {
        return Integer.parseInt(raw);
    }

    // COMPILE ERROR: Method already defined (return type alone cannot overload!)
    // public double parseData(String raw) {
    //     return Double.parseDouble(raw);
    // }

    // Fix by adding a format parameter to overload properly:
    public double parseData(String raw, boolean isDecimal) {
        return Double.parseDouble(raw);
    }
}

practiceProblems.solutionCode:
class DataParser {
    public int parseData(String raw) {
        return Integer.parseInt(raw);
    }
    public double parseData(String raw, boolean isDecimal) {
        return Double.parseDouble(raw);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        DataParser parser = new DataParser();
        System.out.println("Parsed Integer: " + parser.parseData("42"));
        System.out.println("Parsed Double: " + parser.parseData("88.5", true));
    }
}

practiceProblems.problemStatement:
Build a notification hub combining overload and override from scratch:

1. Class NotificationHub:
   - Method 1: public void send(String user, String msg) printing 'Standard Notification to <user>: <msg>'
   - Method 2 (Overload): public void send(String user, String msg, int priority) printing 'Urgent Alert [Priority <priority>] to <user>: <msg>'
   - Method 3 (Overload): public void send(String[] users, String msg) printing 'Broadcast to <users.length> users: <msg>'

2. Class EncryptedNotificationHub (extends NotificationHub):
   - Method (Override): @Override public void send(String user, String msg) printing '[ENCRYPTED-AES256] Dispatch to <user>: <msg>'

Test in Main:
NotificationHub hub = new NotificationHub();
hub.send("Bob", "Meeting at 3pm");
hub.send("Carol", "Server Down", 1);
hub.send(new String[]{"Alice", "Dave"}, "Maintenance tonight");
NotificationHub secureHub = new EncryptedNotificationHub();
secureHub.send("Alice", "Secret Key 9948");.

practiceProblems.solutionCode:
class NotificationHub {
    public void send(String user, String msg) {
        System.out.println("Standard Notification to " + user + ": " + msg);
    }
    public void send(String user, String msg, int priority) {
        System.out.println("Urgent Alert [Priority " + priority + "] to " + user + ": " + msg);
    }
    public void send(String[] users, String msg) {
        System.out.println("Broadcast to " + users.length + " users: " + msg);
    }
}

class SecureNotificationHub extends NotificationHub {
    @Override
    public void send(String user, String msg) {
        System.out.println("[ENCRYPTED-AES256] Dispatch to " + user + ": " + msg);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        NotificationHub hub = new NotificationHub();
        hub.send("Bob", "Meeting at 3pm");
        hub.send("Carol", "Server Down", 1);
        hub.send(new String[]{"Dave", "Eve"}, "Maintenance tonight");

        NotificationHub secure = new SecureNotificationHub();
        secure.send("Alice", "Secret Key 9948");
    }
}
